infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Cost crossover: flat VM vs per-request metering
  desc Sustained traffic favors flat; spiky traffic favors metered — match billing shape to traffic shape
  compares
    - label Self-host — flat VM + CDN
      children
        - label Flat billing, utilization ceiling
          desc Fixed monthly cost regardless of request count
        - label Sustained 60 req/s: ~$50-100/mo
          desc Two 4-vCPU boxes plus CDN egress absorb steady SSR
        - label Spiky 50x press: provision for peak
          desc VM must be sized for the spike and idles the rest of the quarter
        - label You now own the platform work
          desc Shared ISR cache, image pipeline on your CPU, per-PR envs
    - label Vercel — per-request metered
      children
        - label Linear billing in usage
          desc Invocations, GB-hours, image transforms, egress
        - label Sustained 60 req/s: ~10x higher
          desc Metering scales with every request, around the clock
        - label Spiky 50x press: zero capacity planning
          desc Metering absorbs the spike automatically, no provisioning
        - label Sells four hard things
          desc Replicated ISR cache, image fleet, anycast edge, per-PR previews
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
